      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# FieldAid: Offline Disaster Response Copilot",
        "## Gemma 4 Good Hackathon Demo",
        "",
        "Bootstraps FieldAid from scratch and demonstrates the full demo flow: shelter triage, damage assessment, video scanning, trust/grounding, Discord handoff, and offline sync exports — all powered by Gemma 4 (E4B) running locally via Ollama."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 1: Clone the Repository"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!git clone https://github.com/Kushalk0677/fieldaid-offline-disaster-copilot.git --depth 1\n",
        "\n",
        "%cd fieldaid-offline-disaster-copilot\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Repository cloned and changed into directory.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 2: Install Dependencies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip install -r requirements.txt -q\n",
        "\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "print(f\"Python {sys.version}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "from app.main import app\n",
        "print(\"FastAPI app imported successfully.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 3: Install & Start Ollama (Gemma 4 Runtime)\n",
        "",
        "This installs zstd (required by Ollama), then installs Ollama and pulls the `gemma4:e4b` model (~9.6 GB download, 5-10 min). Leave it running."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -y -qq zstd curl > /dev/null 2>&1\n",
        "!curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n",
        "\n",
        "import os, subprocess, time\n",
        "\n",
        "os.system(\"killall -9 ollama 2>/dev/null || true\")\n",
        "print(\"Starting Ollama server...\")\n",
        "subprocess.Popen([\"ollama\", \"serve\"], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)\n",
        "time.sleep(3)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Pulling gemma4:e4b (~9.6 GB). Stand by...\")\n",
        "!ollama pull gemma4:e4b\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Verification:\")\n",
        "!ollama run gemma4:e4b \"Say hello in one word.\" --quiet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!ps aux | grep -i ollama | grep -v grep\n",
        "print(\"---\")\n",
        "!ollama list"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 4: Configure Runtime"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "os.environ[\"FIELDAID_RUNTIME_CACHE\"] = str(Path.home() / \".fieldaid_runtime\")\n",
        "os.environ[\"PYTHONPATH\"] = \".\"\n",
        "\n",
        "Path(\"data/uploads\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "Path(os.environ[\"FIELDAID_RUNTIME_CACHE\"]).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Runtime configured:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Upload dir: {Path('data/uploads').absolute()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Cache: {os.environ['FIELDAID_RUNTIME_CACHE']}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Database: {Path('data/fieldaid.sqlite').absolute()}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "classifier = Path(\"models/fieldaid-medic-image-classifier-final/best.pt\")\n",
        "yolo = Path(\"yolo11n.pt\")\n",
        "for name, p in [(\"Classifier\", classifier), (\"YOLO\", yolo)]:\n",
        "    if p.exists():\n",
        "        print(f\"  {name}: found ({p.stat().st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB)\")\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(f\"  {name}: missing\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 5: Start the Web Server"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os, threading, time\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_server():\n",
        "    os.system(\"uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 > /tmp/fieldaid.log 2>&1\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Starting FieldAid server on port 8000...\")\n",
        "server_thread = threading.Thread(target=run_server, daemon=True)\n",
        "server_thread.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "time.sleep(4)\n",
        "\n",
        "import httpx\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = httpx.get(\"http://localhost:8000\", timeout=5)\n",
        "    print(f\"Server running (status {resp.status_code})\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        from google.colab import output\n",
        "        output.serve_kernel_port_as_window(8000)\n",
        "        print(\"Colab opened the FieldAid server window.\")\n",
        "    except Exception:\n",
        "        print(\"Open http://localhost:8000 if running outside Colab.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"Then click Start Walkthrough button in the bottom-right corner.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "except Exception as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Server not ready yet: {e} (try this cell again)\")\n"
      ]
    }
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 6: Demo Flows"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6A: Shelter Intake"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n",
        "from app.main import app\n",
        "\n",
        "client = TestClient(app)\n",
        "\n",
        "resp = client.post(\n",
        "    \"/api/analyze\",\n",
        "    data={\n",
        "        \"scenario_type\": \"shelter\",\n",
        "        \"note_text\": \"43 people in the school building. 6 elderly residents, 2 insulin patients need refrigeration. Water left for about 8 hours. Bridge to main road is blocked.\",\n",
        "        \"location\": \"Government School, Sector 7\",\n",
        "        \"model\": \"gemma4:e4b\",\n",
        "    },\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "import json\n",
        "if resp.status_code == 200:\n",
        "    d = resp.json()\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(d, indent=2))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(f\"Error {resp.status_code}: {resp.text}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6B: Trust & Grounding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "resp = client.post(\n",
        "    \"/api/grounding\",\n",
        "    data={\n",
        "        \"question\": \"Can civilians safely cross the damaged Creek Road bridge now?\",\n",
        "        \"scenario_type\": \"damage\",\n",
        "        \"model\": \"gemma4:e4b\",\n",
        "    },\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if resp.status_code == 200:\n",
        "    d = resp.json()\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(d, indent=2))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(f\"Error {resp.status_code}: {resp.text}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6C: Dashboard & Incidents"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "dashboard = client.get(\"/api/dashboard\")\n",
        "incidents = client.get(\"/api/incidents\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if dashboard.status_code == 200:\n",
        "    print(\"Dashboard:\")\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(dashboard.json(), indent=2))\n",
        "\n",
        "if incidents.status_code == 200:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nTotal incidents: {len(incidents.json())}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6D: Discord Handoff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "handoff = client.post(\"/api/outbox\", json={\n",
        "    \"incident_id\": 1,\n",
        "    \"channel\": \"discord\",\n",
        "    \"destination\": \"field-response-team\",\n",
        "    \"message\": \"URGENT: 43 people sheltered. Insulin patients need refrigeration. Water running out. Bridge blocked.\",\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "outbox = client.get(\"/api/outbox\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Handoff drafted:\")\n",
        "print(json.dumps(handoff.json(), indent=2))\n",
        "print(f\"\\nOutbox messages: {len(outbox.json())}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6E: Offline Sync Export"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "export = client.get(\"/api/sync/export\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if export.status_code == 200:\n",
        "    data = export.json()\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(data, indent=2))\n",
        "\n",
        "queue = client.get(\"/api/sync/queue\")\n",
        "if queue.status_code == 200:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nSync queue: {len(queue.json())} items\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
